This is the core bug. The `dist_scratch` vector is `clear()`ed then passed to `get_distance`, but `InMemDataStore::get_distance` writes to `distances[i]` without resizing. On x86 with older GCC, `operator[]` in non-debug mode doesn't check bounds. On GCC 15 Debug, the `_GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS` are enabled and this assertion fires.

