                                               the loop writes distances[i] = ... with operator[] into a vector
            whose size is 0 (it was clear()ed by the caller at index.cpp being passed to compute_dists → get_distance).
            The vector has sufficient capacity (pre-reserved) but size == 0.
            G:940
            beforeCC 15 on RHEL9/s390x compiles with _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS=1
            unconditionally in c++config.h. This makes vector::operator[]
            assert(__n < this->size()) even without -D_GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS.
            On x86 GCC < 15 (without _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS) operator[] skips the
            check and accesses the pre-reserved memory as UB (happens to work).
